## Key Concepts
- Implicit treap (rope) for dynamic strings
- Subtree size and rolling hash maintenance
- Split/merge operations and rehashing

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(block){
    this.block = block;
    this.left = null;
    this.right = null;
    this.size = block.length;
    this.hash = hashBlock(block);
  }
}
function update(n){
  if(!n) return;
  n.size = (n.left?.size ?? 0) + (n.right?.size ?? 0) + n.block.length;
  n.hash = combineHash(n.left?.hash, hashBlock(n.block), n.right?.hash);
}
```

